In these variables the energy is simply $H=-J\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\mu_i.$ The interacting site variables have become independent bond variables. Summing first over the two values of $\sigma_1$ gives $\begin{aligned}
Z_N
&=2\sum_{\{\mu_i=\pm1\}}
\exp\left(\beta J\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\mu_i\right)\\
&=2\prod_{i=1}^{N-1}
\left(\sum_{\mu_i=\pm1}e^{\beta J\mu_i}\right)\\
&=2\left[2\cosh(\beta J)\right]^{N-1}.
\end{aligned}$ There are $N-1$ factors because an open chain of $N$ sites has $N-1$ bonds.

