p.src:
For spins separated by $r$ bonds, $\begin{aligned}
\sigma_i\sigma_{i+r}
&=\sigma_i
\left(\prod_{k=i+1}^{i+r-1}\sigma_k^2\right)
\sigma_{i+r}\\
&=(\sigma_i\sigma_{i+1})
(\sigma_{i+1}\sigma_{i+2})\cdots
(\sigma_{i+r-1}\sigma_{i+r})\\
&=\prod_{k=i}^{i+r-1}\mu_k.\end{aligned}$ Because the $\mu_k$ are independent, $C(r)=\expect{\sigma_i\sigma_{i+r}}
=\left[\tanh(\beta J)\right]^r.$

