p.src:
The corresponding free energy makes the tilt visible: $f_{\rm MF}(m;h)
=dJm^2-\frac{1}{\beta}
\log\!\left[2\cosh\!\left(\beta(2dJm+h)\right)\right].$ At $h=0$ the two wells are equally deep. A positive $h$ lowers the positive-$m$ well and raises the negative-$m$ well. The perturbation per spin can be tiny while the total preference, multiplied by $N$, is macroscopic.

